* @title Unevaluated BREAK argument uses the current character
* @attribution Griswold 1971, Chapter 2, Section 2.16
* @input >>>
* TWO STRINGS FOR TESTING
* ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ
* <<<
* @expect TWOSTRINGSFORTESTING
          &ANCHOR = 1; &TRIM = 1
          CHAR = LEN(1) . CH
          FINDCH = BREAK(*CH)
          STRING1 = INPUT :F(ERROR)
          STRING2 = INPUT :F(ERROR)
LOOP      STRING1 CHAR = :F(OUTPUT)
          STRING2 FINDCH :F(LOOP)
          LIST = LIST CH :(LOOP)
OUTPUT    OUTPUT = LIST
END
